# before: resolve.sh f32d587c33264a392e09028b1a0f71c5daa2c589ec80a51a491c584549230a54 (399 lines); build_cake_lpr.sh 3813e60e7dc5feed9b864c5cee3186450a52cce2229a89c7335093fbfe20bdf7 (53 lines)
# after:  resolve.sh 22e07b3be34f49f3823bd12e4dfdb02350edacb66dceaace329ab20bd21059e0 (611 lines); build_cake_lpr.sh 488502baa677c954badfe24b4ffc78dcb2c3a03c169fe287f1205bc2dbfaf12d (87 lines)
# bash -n: rc 0 on both; shellcheck 0.11.0 (default severity) on both: rc 0, no findings.
# What changed, by defect (D1-D10 as numbered in m9_review_resolve.log):
#  D1  summary: every requested cube's current row, written now or earlier, is checked again (verdict, cadical_rc 20, cake_rc 0, exact cake_line,
#      cnf_records, rehash_after_cake, cnf_sha256 vs both records loaded by THIS run, P.cnf hash, P.lrat size (+ full hash for rows of earlier runs),
#      P.cake.log single exact s-line) and counts toward PASS only if its cake_sha256 is the PINNED hash; with RS_UNPINNED_CAKE=1 such rows give
#      verdict UNPINNED and exit 3, never PASS; the SUMMARY line reports skipped/incomplete/unpinned counts.
#  D2  P.cnf and P.lrat are chmod a-w once written and hashed again AFTER cake_lpr (column rehash_after_cake); any change -> FILE-CHANGED, not ACCEPTED.
#  D3  each tool is copied to OUTDIR/tools/<sha256>/<name> (0555) and only the copy runs; its hash is checked before each cube, before each CaDiCaL and
#      cake_lpr run (TOOL-CHANGED + stop otherwise) and at the end; the exe_sha256 column is the snapshot's hash, whatever happens to .lake later.
#  D4  RS_EXE/RS_CADICAL/RS_CAKE (and the record overrides) are resolved with realpath against the caller's directory before the cd, never via PATH;
#      the pin is decided on the hash before any tool runs; --version runs only on a pinned or explicitly allowed binary, under RS_CAP_CADICAL.
#  D5  verdicts split: SAT (rc 10), CADICAL-KILLED/CAKE-KILLED/EMIT-KILLED (rc >= 128), *-ERROR (other rc; cake_lpr 1/2/3 = heap/stack/runtime),
#      REJECTED only for cake_lpr rc 0 without the exact line; the non-result verdicts are retryable: a plain rerun reports INCOMPLETE, RS_RETRY=1
#      starts attempt K+1 under OUTDIR/NAME.tryK (new column attempt), keeping attempt K's files and row; results.tsv stays append-only.
#  D6  sha() hashes stdin (sha256sum < FILE), so no path escaping can corrupt the hash; OUTDIR with a control character is refused.
#  D7  RS_TCTL_MAX must be a number in 50..84, RS_MIN_FREE_GB a whole number >= 400 (10# base; no arithmetic on raw input); RS_RELAX_LIMITS=1
#      widens to 50..100 / >= 0 (logged); 0/1 switches are validated; the free-space check uses bytes (df -B1) against GiB.
#  D8  build_cake_lpr.sh runs make under env -i PATH=/usr/bin:/bin LC_ALL=C TMPDIR=WORKDIR/tmp and requires make's printed command to be exactly
#      'cc -O2 basis_ffi.c cake_lpr.S -o cake_lpr'.
#  D9  build_cake_lpr.sh compares Makefile/basis_ffi.c/cake_lpr.S with sha256 pins (written in the script; verified from the host clone, and the
#      cake_lpr.S prefix d20ceae0 must appear in the replay README) before make; mismatch = exit 2.
#  D10 build_cake_lpr.sh WORKDIR [REPO]: REPO may be a local clone; if the commit is not among the cloned refs it is fetched by full id.
# results.tsv now has 23 columns (new: attempt after index, rehash_after_cake after cake_maxrss_kb); a directory with the old 21-column header is
# refused (exit 2), so the old smoke dir resolve-smoke is not reused.
#
## (A) stub tests: no solver or checker ran; every CaDiCaL/cake_lpr below is a stub script unless the line says otherwise (S2/S3/F2/F2b use the real
